# Tracker docs are governed by `npm run lint:progress` (80 KB cap + live-state
# contract in scripts/check-progress-doc.mjs), NOT by Prettier. Prettier's Markdown
# table padding inflates PROGRESS.md to 66 KB -- 4.8 KB past the hard cap. CLAUDE.md
# is loaded into every session and every teammate spawn; padding is a context tax.
# Rotation targets stay under the same regime so verbatim moves stay byte-identical.
PROGRESS.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/progress/
# ADR 0185 moved the registers out of docs/progress/ and added hubs; the same regime applies
# (the follow-up register has no cap BY DECISION, the others are gated for shape, and the
# hubs' Current-state blocks are line-capped at 60 — padding eats that headroom too).
docs/followups/
docs/bugs/
docs/learning/
docs/features/
docs/planning/

# The ADR index is GENERATED byte-for-byte by scripts/build-adr-index.mjs and
# byte-compared by `npm run lint:adr-index` (gate 9). Prettier's Markdown table padding
# would rewrite it into something the generator never emits, so `npm run format` would
# red the gate and the "fix" would be to regenerate -- undoing the formatting. The two
# tools cannot both own this file; the gate does.
docs/decisions/INDEX.md

# CONTEXT.md is the domain glossary, edited inline term-by-term by the
# domain-modeling skill. Prettier renormalizes its emphasis and wrapping, which
# churns the diff of every such edit and obscures which term actually changed.
CONTEXT.md
